<DocsLayout
  title="Registries"
  description="Independent sources that publish extension information and releases."
>
  <h2>Responsibility</h2>
  <p>
    A registry is responsible for the extension information it publishes and
    the infrastructure used to distribute releases. ExtensionMesh does not
    require all registries to be operated by one organization.
  </p>

  <h2>What independence means</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The operator controls the registry infrastructure and availability.</li>
    <li>The operator decides which extensions are published.</li>
    <li>Authentication and access rules may be specific to that registry.</li>
    <li>A connector can consume more than one compatible registry source.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Current documentation scope</h2>
  <p>
    The project does not yet publish a stable universal registry
    specification. The first implementation is being used to identify which
    metadata, release and authentication behaviors are genuinely shared.
  </p>

  <div class="notice">
    <strong>Implementation-led</strong>
    <p>
      If you operate or plan an independent registry, concrete requirements and
      edge cases are more useful now than speculative completeness.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Useful contribution topics</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Real publication and release workflows.</li>
    <li>Authentication and entitlement requirements.</li>
    <li>Version compatibility and dependency metadata.</li>
    <li>Failure behavior, availability and caching.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
